@lang en
IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT domain
IMPORT `g6-nouns`
IMPORT `g6-schedule-three`
IMPORT `g6-notice-and-hearing`
IMPORT `g6-amount`

-- ind-c-tests-amount.l4: independent tests (ind-c) of ss.45, 46 and 47 (gazette p. 194).
-- Scenario ids are those of work/ind-c/expectations.md, decided from the source before the encoding was opened.
-- Money in new shekels.  Where no index update is meant, the first update year is put after the day asked
-- about, so the fixed amount is the amount as enacted (the first update day is an input: the Law does not name it).

§ `ind-c: ss 45 to 47`

§§ `Fixtures`

`ind-c individual` MEANS Person WITH `reference for the person` IS "ind-1", `kind of person` IS `an individual`
`ind-c corporation` MEANS Person WITH `reference for the person` IS "corp-1", `kind of person` IS `a corporation`
`ind-c another individual` MEANS Person WITH `reference for the person` IS "ind-2", `kind of person` IS `an individual`

GIVEN who IS A Person
      what IS A `Listed violation`
      day IS A DATE
GIVETH A Violation
`ind-c violation by` who `of` what `on` day MEANS
    Violation WITH `the violator` IS who
                 , `the listed violation` IS what
                 , `reference for the act` IS "act-new"
                 , `date of the act` IS day

GIVEN who IS A Person
      what IS A `Listed violation`
      day IS A DATE
      wasSanctioned IS A BOOLEAN
      wasConvicted IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `Previous violation`
`ind-c previous violation by` who `of` what `on` day `sanctioned` wasSanctioned `convicted` wasConvicted MEANS
    `Previous violation` WITH `the violator` IS who
                            , `the listed violation` IS what
                            , `date of the act` IS day
                            , `a financial sanction was imposed for it` IS wasSanctioned
                            , `the violator was convicted for it` IS wasConvicted

`no index readings` MEANS EMPTY

-- The sanction on 2027-06-01 with the first update in 2028: no update has happened.
GIVEN v IS A Violation
      n IS A NUMBER
      isRepeat IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A NUMBER
`ind-c sanction, no update, for` v `continuing months` n `repeat` isRepeat MEANS
    `s 45 to 47 — the financial sanction for the violation` v n isRepeat (YMD 2027 6 1) 2028 `no index readings`

§§ `C1-C9: the additions of s 45`

-- C1: item (1), individual, continuing 3 whole months: 20,000 + 3 x 400.
#ASSERT `ind-c sanction, no update, for` (`ind-c violation by` `ind-c individual` `of` `work with no licence at all` `on` (YMD 2027 3 10)) `continuing months` 3 `repeat` FALSE EQUALS 21200
-- C2: item (3), individual, 1 month: 5,000 + 100.
#ASSERT `ind-c sanction, no update, for` (`ind-c violation by` `ind-c individual` `of` `advertising as licensed without the licence or the kind` `on` (YMD 2027 3 10)) `continuing months` 1 `repeat` FALSE EQUALS 5100
-- C3: item (7), corporation, 2 months: 6,000 + 2 x 120.
#ASSERT `ind-c sanction, no update, for` (`ind-c violation by` `ind-c corporation` `of` `failing to give a document an inspector demanded` `on` (YMD 2027 3 10)) `continuing months` 2 `repeat` FALSE EQUALS 6240
-- C4: item (5), corporation, 12 months: 40,000 + 12 x 800 (above the s.41(b) cap, which binds orders only).
#ASSERT `ind-c sanction, no update, for` (`ind-c violation by` `ind-c corporation` `of` `engaging a person who had no licence at all` `on` (YMD 2027 3 10)) `continuing months` 12 `repeat` FALSE EQUALS 49600
-- C5: item (6), corporation, repeat: 20,000 + 20,000.
#ASSERT `ind-c sanction, no update, for` (`ind-c violation by` `ind-c corporation` `of` `engaging a person without a licence of the appropriate kind` `on` (YMD 2027 3 10)) `continuing months` 0 `repeat` TRUE EQUALS 40000
-- C6: item (7), individual, repeat: 3,000 + 3,000.
#ASSERT `ind-c sanction, no update, for` (`ind-c violation by` `ind-c individual` `of` `failing to give a document an inspector demanded` `on` (YMD 2027 3 10)) `continuing months` 0 `repeat` TRUE EQUALS 6000
-- C7: neither continuing nor repeat: item (2), individual, 10,000.
#ASSERT `ind-c sanction, no update, for` (`ind-c violation by` `ind-c individual` `of` `work without a licence of the kind appropriate to the system` `on` (YMD 2027 3 10)) `continuing months` 0 `repeat` FALSE EQUALS 10000
-- C9: item (1), individual, repeat AND 3 months continuing: 20,000 + 20,000 + 1,200 (each addition on the fixed sanction).
#ASSERT `ind-c sanction, no update, for` (`ind-c violation by` `ind-c individual` `of` `work with no licence at all` `on` (YMD 2027 3 10)) `continuing months` 3 `repeat` TRUE EQUALS 41200
-- B8: that total exceeds 40,000, and the cap of s.41(b) does not bound it.
#ASSERT `ind-c sanction, no update, for` (`ind-c violation by` `ind-c individual` `of` `work with no licence at all` `on` (YMD 2027 3 10)) `continuing months` 3 `repeat` TRUE GREATER THAN 40000
-- The pieces.
#ASSERT `s 45(a) — the addition of one fiftieth of` 20000 `for each of the months` 3 EQUALS 1200
#ASSERT `s 45(a) — the addition of one fiftieth of` 6000 `for each of the months` 2 EQUALS 240
#ASSERT `s 45(b) — the addition for a repeat violation of` 10000 `where` TRUE EQUALS 10000
#ASSERT `s 45(b) — the addition for a repeat violation of` 10000 `where` FALSE EQUALS 0
-- Whole months of continuation (my scenarios use whole months; part months are ambiguity X3):
-- from 2027-03-10 to 2027-06-10 is three whole months; to 2027-06-09, two.
#ASSERT `s 45(a) — the whole months a violation continued from` (YMD 2027 3 10) `to` (YMD 2027 6 10) EQUALS 3
#ASSERT `s 45(a) — the whole months a violation continued from` (YMD 2027 3 10) `to` (YMD 2027 6 9) EQUALS 2

§§ `C8, C10-C15: what makes a repeat violation (s 45(b))`

-- C8: the previous violation of the same provision ended in neither a sanction nor a conviction: not a repeat.
#ASSERT NOT (`s 45(b) — the violation` (`ind-c violation by` `ind-c individual` `of` `work with no licence at all` `on` (YMD 2028 1 10)) `is a repeat violation, given` (LIST (`ind-c previous violation by` `ind-c individual` `of` `work with no licence at all` `on` (YMD 2027 3 10) `sanctioned` FALSE `convicted` FALSE)))
-- A conviction instead of a sanction is enough.
#ASSERT `s 45(b) — the violation` (`ind-c violation by` `ind-c individual` `of` `work with no licence at all` `on` (YMD 2028 1 10)) `is a repeat violation, given` (LIST (`ind-c previous violation by` `ind-c individual` `of` `work with no licence at all` `on` (YMD 2027 3 10) `sanctioned` FALSE `convicted` TRUE))
-- C10: previous violation 2027-03-10, sanctioned; new 2029-03-10: the last day of the two years, a repeat.
#ASSERT `s 45(b) — the violation` (`ind-c violation by` `ind-c individual` `of` `work with no licence at all` `on` (YMD 2029 3 10)) `is a repeat violation, given` (LIST (`ind-c previous violation by` `ind-c individual` `of` `work with no licence at all` `on` (YMD 2027 3 10) `sanctioned` TRUE `convicted` FALSE))
-- C11: new 2029-03-11: not a repeat.
#ASSERT NOT (`s 45(b) — the violation` (`ind-c violation by` `ind-c individual` `of` `work with no licence at all` `on` (YMD 2029 3 11)) `is a repeat violation, given` (LIST (`ind-c previous violation by` `ind-c individual` `of` `work with no licence at all` `on` (YMD 2027 3 10) `sanctioned` TRUE `convicted` FALSE)))
-- C12: previous 2028-02-29; new 2030-02-28 (February 2030 lacks the 29th): a repeat.
#ASSERT `s 45(b) — the violation` (`ind-c violation by` `ind-c individual` `of` `failing to give a document an inspector demanded` `on` (YMD 2030 2 28)) `is a repeat violation, given` (LIST (`ind-c previous violation by` `ind-c individual` `of` `failing to give a document an inspector demanded` `on` (YMD 2028 2 29) `sanctioned` TRUE `convicted` FALSE))
-- C13: new 2030-03-01: not a repeat.
#ASSERT NOT (`s 45(b) — the violation` (`ind-c violation by` `ind-c individual` `of` `failing to give a document an inspector demanded` `on` (YMD 2030 3 1)) `is a repeat violation, given` (LIST (`ind-c previous violation by` `ind-c individual` `of` `failing to give a document an inspector demanded` `on` (YMD 2028 2 29) `sanctioned` TRUE `convicted` FALSE)))
-- The window's last day through the encoding's helper.
#ASSERT `s 45(b) — the last day of the two years from the previous violation` (`ind-c previous violation by` `ind-c individual` `of` `failing to give a document an inspector demanded` `on` (YMD 2028 2 29) `sanctioned` TRUE `convicted` FALSE) EQUALS YMD 2030 2 28
#ASSERT `s 45(b) — the last day of the two years from the previous violation` (`ind-c previous violation by` `ind-c individual` `of` `work with no licence at all` `on` (YMD 2027 3 10) `sanctioned` TRUE `convicted` FALSE) EQUALS YMD 2029 3 10
-- C14: a different provision (previous s.4, item (3); new s.18(a), item (5)), within the window: not a repeat.
#ASSERT NOT (`s 45(b) — the violation` (`ind-c violation by` `ind-c individual` `of` `engaging a person who had no licence at all` `on` (YMD 2028 1 10)) `is a repeat violation, given` (LIST (`ind-c previous violation by` `ind-c individual` `of` `advertising as licensed without the licence or the kind` `on` (YMD 2027 3 10) `sanctioned` TRUE `convicted` FALSE)))
-- C15: the previous violation on 2027-03-01 (sanctioned later, in 2028); the new one on 2029-04-01 is more than two
-- years after the previous VIOLATION: not a repeat.
#ASSERT NOT (`s 45(b) — the violation` (`ind-c violation by` `ind-c individual` `of` `work with no licence at all` `on` (YMD 2029 4 1)) `is a repeat violation, given` (LIST (`ind-c previous violation by` `ind-c individual` `of` `work with no licence at all` `on` (YMD 2027 3 1) `sanctioned` TRUE `convicted` FALSE)))
-- Another person's earlier violation does not make this one a repeat.
#ASSERT NOT (`s 45(b) — the violation` (`ind-c violation by` `ind-c individual` `of` `work with no licence at all` `on` (YMD 2028 1 10)) `is a repeat violation, given` (LIST (`ind-c previous violation by` `ind-c another individual` `of` `work with no licence at all` `on` (YMD 2027 3 10) `sanctioned` TRUE `convicted` FALSE)))
-- X2 (ambiguity, both readings checked): item (2) within two years after a sanctioned item (1), both under s.3(a).
-- Section reading: a repeat; row reading: not.
#ASSERT `s 45(b) — the previous violation makes the violation a repeat violation` (`ind-c violation by` `ind-c individual` `of` `work without a licence of the kind appropriate to the system` `on` (YMD 2028 1 10)) (`ind-c previous violation by` `ind-c individual` `of` `work with no licence at all` `on` (YMD 2027 3 10) `sanctioned` TRUE `convicted` FALSE)
#ASSERT NOT (`s 45(b) — the previous violation, read by Third Schedule item, makes the violation a repeat violation` (`ind-c violation by` `ind-c individual` `of` `work without a licence of the kind appropriate to the system` `on` (YMD 2028 1 10)) (`ind-c previous violation by` `ind-c individual` `of` `work with no licence at all` `on` (YMD 2027 3 10) `sanctioned` TRUE `convicted` FALSE))

§§ `C16-C17: s 46, no amount below the fixed amounts unless under s 46(b)`

-- C16: no s.46(b) rules relied on: the lowest sanction is the fixed amount; 15,000 for a 20,000 item is below it.
#ASSERT `s 46 — the lowest sanction the Commissioner may impose` 20000 FALSE NOTHING EQUALS 20000
#ASSERT NOT (`s 46(a) — a sanction of` 15000 `is not lower than the amounts fixed, which are` 20000)
#ASSERT `s 46(a) — a sanction of` 20000 `is not lower than the amounts fixed, which are` 20000
-- C17: s.46(b) rules allow a reduction of a quarter (the rate is the rules' content, an input): 15,000 is allowed.
#ASSERT `s 46 — the lowest sanction the Commissioner may impose` 20000 TRUE (JUST 0.25) EQUALS 15000
#ASSERT `s 46(a) — a sanction of` 15000 `is not lower than the amounts fixed, which are` (`s 46 — the lowest sanction the Commissioner may impose` 20000 TRUE (JUST 0.25))

§§ `C19-C21: s 47(a), the day of the updated amount`

-- C19: the violator argued; the demand was delivered 2028-01-25: that day.
#ASSERT `s 47(a) — the day on which the amount of the sanction is updated` (YMD 2027 12 20) TRUE (JUST (YMD 2028 1 25)) FALSE NOTHING EQUALS JUST (YMD 2028 1 25)
-- C20: the violator did not argue: the day the notice of intention was delivered, 2027-12-20, not the deemed
-- demand of 2028-01-19.
#ASSERT `s 47(a) — the day on which the amount of the sanction is updated` (YMD 2027 12 20) FALSE (JUST (YMD 2028 1 19)) FALSE NOTHING EQUALS JUST (YMD 2027 12 20)
-- C21: appeal filed and payment stayed: the day of the decision in the appeal.
#ASSERT `s 47(a) — the day on which the amount of the sanction is updated` (YMD 2027 12 20) TRUE (JUST (YMD 2028 1 25)) TRUE (JUST (YMD 2028 9 1)) EQUALS JUST (YMD 2028 9 1)

§§ `C22-C26: s 47(b), the update by the index, rounded to the nearest NIS 10`

-- The index known on 1 January 2027 is 100 (the November 2026 reading); known on 1 January 2028 is the November 2027
-- reading, whose value each test chooses.  The first update day is 1 January 2028.
GIVEN newValue IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A LIST OF `Price index reading`
`ind-c readings rising to` newValue MEANS
    LIST (`Price index reading` WITH `year of the index` IS 2026, `month of the index` IS 11, `published on` IS YMD 2026 12 15, `value of the index` IS 100)
       , (`Price index reading` WITH `year of the index` IS 2027, `month of the index` IS 11, `published on` IS YMD 2027 12 15, `value of the index` IS newValue)

-- C22: 3,000 x 1.017 = 3,051 -> 3,050.
#ASSERT `s 47(b) — the amount of` 3000 `updated on` (YMD 2028 3 1) `, the first update being in` 2028 `and the index readings being` (`ind-c readings rising to` 101.7) EQUALS 3050
-- C23: 20,000 x 1.0249 = 20,498 -> 20,500.
#ASSERT `s 47(b) — the amount of` 20000 `updated on` (YMD 2028 3 1) `, the first update being in` 2028 `and the index readings being` (`ind-c readings rising to` 102.49) EQUALS 20500
-- C24: 10,000 x 1.0236 = 10,236 -> 10,240.
#ASSERT `s 47(b) — the amount of` 10000 `updated on` (YMD 2028 3 1) `, the first update being in` 2028 `and the index readings being` (`ind-c readings rising to` 102.36) EQUALS 10240
-- C25: 6,000 x 1.0184 = 6,110.4 -> 6,110.
#ASSERT `s 47(b) — the amount of` 6000 `updated on` (YMD 2028 3 1) `, the first update being in` 2028 `and the index readings being` (`ind-c readings rising to` 101.84) EQUALS 6110
-- C26: a falling index, 100 -> 99: 20,000 -> 19,800.
#ASSERT `s 47(b) — the amount of` 20000 `updated on` (YMD 2028 3 1) `, the first update being in` 2028 `and the index readings being` (`ind-c readings rising to` 99) EQUALS 19800
-- On 31 December 2027 the 2028 update has not happened: 3,000.
#ASSERT `s 47(b) — the amount of` 3000 `updated on` (YMD 2027 12 31) `, the first update being in` 2028 `and the index readings being` (`ind-c readings rising to` 101.7) EQUALS 3000
-- The nearest-10 rounding on its own (not the nearest shekel of the Fees Regulations' reg 3): 3,051 -> 3,050, not 3,051.
#ASSERT `s 47(b) — the nearest multiple of NIS 10 to` 3051 EQUALS 3050
#ASSERT `s 47(b) — the nearest multiple of NIS 10 to` 3056 EQUALS 3060

-- C20 carried through to the amount: notice 2027-12-20, no arguments, 1 January 2028 update of 1.7 per cent:
-- item (7) for an individual stays at 3,000 (the 2027 amount), because s.47(a) fixes the notice's day.
#ASSERT `s 45 to 47 — the financial sanction for the violation` (`ind-c violation by` `ind-c individual` `of` `failing to give a document an inspector demanded` `on` (YMD 2027 11 1)) 0 FALSE (YMD 2027 12 20) 2028 (`ind-c readings rising to` 101.7) EQUALS 3000
-- C19 carried through: had he argued and the demand been delivered 2028-01-25, the 2028 amount, 3,050.
#ASSERT `s 45 to 47 — the financial sanction for the violation` (`ind-c violation by` `ind-c individual` `of` `failing to give a document an inspector demanded` `on` (YMD 2027 11 1)) 0 FALSE (YMD 2028 1 25) 2028 (`ind-c readings rising to` 101.7) EQUALS 3050

§§ `X3, X6: the ambiguities of ss 45(a) and 47(b), both readings checked`

-- X3: a violation from 2027-03-10 to 2027-04-25 (one and a half months): one whole month on the reading taken, two
-- calendar months touched on the other, one calendar month after the first on the third.
#ASSERT `s 45(a) — the whole months a violation continued from` (YMD 2027 3 10) `to` (YMD 2027 4 25) EQUALS 1
#ASSERT `s 45(a) — the calendar months touched by a violation from` (YMD 2027 3 10) `to` (YMD 2027 4 25) EQUALS 2
#ASSERT `s 45(a) — the calendar months touched after the first, by a violation from` (YMD 2027 3 10) `to` (YMD 2027 4 25) EQUALS 1
-- X6: a half-way amount, 5,125: 5,130 rounding a half up, 5,120 rounding it to the even multiple.
#ASSERT `s 47(b) — the nearest multiple of NIS 10 to` 5125 EQUALS 5130
#ASSERT `s 47(b) — the nearest multiple of NIS 10, a half going to the even multiple, to` 5125 EQUALS 5120
-- X5: repeat and continuing together: the reading taken adds 1/50 of the FIXED sanction (C9, 41,200); the other reading
-- (1/50 of the doubled sanction, 42,400) has no function in the encoding.
